Data Preprocessing Across Multiple Domains  
(IPL, Flipkart, Spotify, Zomato, BookMyShow)

Task 1: IPL Player Stats – StandardScaler

Code:
import pandas as pd
from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler
df = pd.read_csv("ipl_stats.csv")
features = ["runs", "wickets", "matches", "strike_rate"]
X = df[features]
scaler = StandardScaler()
X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)
scaled_df = pd.DataFrame(X_scaled, columns=features)
scaled_df.to_csv("ipl_scaled.csv", index=False)
print("Scaled data:")
print(scaled_df.head())

Answe:
StandardScaler transforms numeric features to have mean = 0 and standard deviation = 1.  
This ensures fair contribution of all stats in ML models.  

Task 2: Flipkart Product Ratings – MinMaxScaler

Code:
import pandas as pd
from sklearn.preprocessing import MinMaxScaler
df = pd.read_csv("flipkart_products.csv")
features = ["price", "rating", "number_of_reviews", "discount"]
X = df[features]
print("Before Scaling:\n", X.min(), "\n", X.max())
scaler = MinMaxScaler()
X_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X)
scaled_df = pd.DataFrame(X_scaled, columns=features)
print("After Scaling:\n", scaled_df.min(), "\n", scaled_df.max())

Answe:
MinMaxScaler rescales values into the range [0,1].  
After scaling → min = 0, max = 1 for each feature.  

