Task 4: Zomato Restaurants – RFE Feature Selection

Code:
import pandas as pd
from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeRegressor
from sklearn.feature_selection import RFE
df = pd.read_csv("zomato.csv")
features = ["votes", "rating", "price_range", "table_booking", "online_order"]
X = df[features]
y = df["average_cost_for_two"]
model = DecisionTreeRegressor(random_state=42)
rfe = RFE(estimator=model, n_features_to_select=3)
rfe.fit(X, y)
selected_features = X.columns[rfe.support_]
print("Selected Features:\n", selected_features)
print("\nRFE Ranking:")
for feature, rank in zip(X.columns, rfe.ranking_):
    print(feature, "=", rank)


Answer:
RFE eliminates less important features iteratively.  
Example selected features: rating, votes, price_range.  
Exact output depends on dataset.

Task 5: BookMyShow Movie Ratings – Outlier Detection (IQR)

Code:
import pandas as pd
df = pd.read_csv("bookmyshow_movies.csv")
Q1 = df["user ratings"].quantile(0.25)
Q3 = df["user ratings"].quantile(0.75)
IQR = Q3 - Q1
lower_limit = Q1 - 1.5 * IQR
upper_limit = Q3 + 1.5 * IQR
df_clean = df[(df["user ratings"] >= lower_limit) & (df["user ratings"] <= upper_limit)]
rows_dropped = len(df) - len(df_clean)
print("Rows dropped:", rows_dropped)
print("Rows remaining:", len(df_clean))

Answer:
IQR method removes extreme values outside \([Q1 - 1.5×IQR, Q3 + 1.5×IQR]\).  
This ensures cleaner, more reliable data for modeling.  
